A||N||1||DaRkLoRD||Got an email with some questions, can anyone help answer them?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||07-29-2000||02:06 PM||||I received this email. and I'm afraid I can't answer any of this stuff.. but I KNOW you guys can.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Hi there,<BR>I am about knee deep into my 86 2.8 rebuild and I have some questions for you that I am hoping that you can help me with. I would very much like to convert my 2.8 into a 3.1 but I am having some problems. I found on the internet on the Fiero online service guide that there are only certain 2.8 ltr blocks that can be used for this conversion and mine doesn't seem to be one of them. Instead of one of the 3 "approved" codes, 2.8 with DAF, DAH or DBN, on the side of the block, mine has "2.8 LG". Presumably this is for 2.8 liters, Large Journal. Are you familiar with this code and can you tell me if it will work with the 3.1 liter crank? I have been told that the reason is that the 3.1 crank has a crank trigger lobe that will interfere with certain blocks. My block is being bored out as I type this so I don't have much time to order the other parts that I need. Also do you know if the standard 3.1 ltr pistons for the cast iron 3.1 ltr heads will work in my engine with this combo? Also do you seel any kits that would do what I am trying to do? Any help that you could give would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thank you very much.<P>Brian<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE></B><P>This guy's email address is  <A HREF="mailto:pdqfiero@yahoo.com">pdqfiero@yahoo.com</A> <P>I'll point him towards the forum, but if anyone could email this guy some quick answers to his questions.. that'd be great. thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||squid||07-30-2000||08:48 PM||||I dont know about the specific engine codes. I do know that the early 2.8's had smaller main journals which is the reason they wont work with a stock 3.1 crank. If you have the large journal block then you wont have a problem. The timing ring wont hit anything. I used pistons for a 1992 firebird with a 3.1. The rear wheel drive vehicles had cast iron heads. I used a crank for a 1989 Pontiac 6000 STE (first year of the 3.1).If your stock, unturned,crank measures between 2.6473" and 2.6483" then you can use a 3.1 crank.||||reg||1
